WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00.000 --> 00:12.000
All right. One thing I see a lot of is the use of blank lines to create whitespace between paragraphs of text or before an image, etc.

00:12.000 --> 00:22.000
So in this example, I have a paragraph of text. I have about four or five blank lines and then an image. I'm going to delete these blank lines.

00:22.000 --> 00:37.000
And to create the space I want, I go to the Home tab under the Paragraph section, and there's line and paragraph spacing.

00:37.000 --> 00:46.000
I change the line spacing options, and under the option here "Spacing before or after", in this case, I'm going to adjust the spacing after the paragraph I'm on.

00:46.000 --> 01:03.000
And I'm going to give it anywhere from 15 points or 20 points. In this case, there were four blank lines, so I'm going to do about 50 points to get that spacing that I want.

01:03.000 --> 01:17.000
And now I have complete separation between the image and without any blank lines with the paragraph before it.